Correction 1 - normalized fault PC: the V3 report/audit say normalized-PC agreement
is false and later say both cores have the same raw PC. Both are wrong. The raw
PCs are 0x5583c3fc3ee0 (V1) and 0x558245244ee0 (V2); subtracting their respective
load bases 0x5583c3962000 (V1) and 0x558244be3000 (V2) gives 0x661ee0 for BOTH.
The normalized fault offset agreement is TRUE; the raw PCs differ only under ASLR.

Correction 2 - fault-path candidate: the V3 report's SMPfindElt NULL-dereference
candidate is RETRACTED. The patched source dereferences sd_ctx->elt2 only when it
is non-NULL (a conditional guard); the cores therefore do not establish that
candidate. The exact source/function mapping of offset 0x661ee0 and the precise
crash chain remain PROVISIONAL.

Correction 3 - dependency count: the V3 claims section's unresolved '%d Tpo files'
is the direct count 1,085 dependency files (.Plo/.Po/.Tpo). That is a dependency-
cone INVENTORY, not proof that every listed object was linked. Linked-input claims
bind only to the accepted LINK-V5 inventory (the retained link command's inputs).

